# DIY Vertical Monitor Rail (Friction-Locking System)

This design uses industrial steel linear rails (like those found in CNC machines) to provide a smooth vertical track behind your desk. It completely eliminates springs, pulleys, and gas struts, making it impossible to jam or snap. To use it, you simply loosen a quick-release knob, slide the monitor up or down with your hands, and lock it back into place.

